  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Pedro Padilla helped rebuild consumer lending at Mexican retailer Elektra after a currency crisis had forced the company to withdraw credit. He restored instalment purchasing and developed financial services for customers, alongside information systems supporting new stores and retail formats. At TV Azteca, his cash-distribution programme combined debt reduction with payments to shareholders.\n\nHis interest in Mexican spirits also led him to support a publishing project. When writer Francisco Martín Moreno and photographer Ignacio Urquiza proposed collecting stories heard by bartenders, Padilla wanted Loco Tequila involved. Their visits to bars in Mexico and the United States produced a book containing fourteen stories, with a cover by artist Ricardo Fernández.",
    "html": "<p>Pedro Padilla helped rebuild consumer lending at Mexican retailer Elektra after a currency crisis had forced the company to withdraw credit. He restored instalment purchasing and developed financial services for customers, alongside information systems supporting new stores and retail formats. At TV Azteca, his cash-distribution programme combined debt reduction with payments to shareholders.</p>\r\n<p>His interest in Mexican spirits also led him to support a publishing project. When writer Francisco Martín Moreno and photographer Ignacio Urquiza proposed collecting stories heard by bartenders, Padilla wanted Loco Tequila involved. Their visits to bars in Mexico and the United States produced a book containing fourteen stories, with a cover by artist Ricardo Fernández.</p>\r\n",
    "word_count": 109,
